<title>GREECE: BEFORE THE BELL - STOCKS TRADING EX-DIV MONDAY.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - STOCKS TRADING EX-DIV MONDAY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens stock exchange said</p>
<p>shares of tobacco firm Karelia , cement producer Halyps</p>
<p>and Katselis will trade ex-dividend on Monday.</p>
<p>    Company     Dividend/share   Coupon    Ex-div opening price</p>
<p>    Katselis     100 drachmas	9	    1,630  common</p>
<p>							    1,400  preferred</p>
<p>    Halyps	  22.36 drachmas   3		647  preferred</p>
<p>    Karelia	101 drachmas	2	    5,249</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
